          "worked": "Write $x=10^y$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}10^{-2}&=0.01\\\\10^{-1}&=0.1\\\\10^0&=1\\\\10^1&=10\\\\10^2&=100\\end{align*}$$\n\nPlot $(0.01,-2)$, $(0.1,-1)$, $(1,0)$, $(10,1)$ and $(100,2)$. Join them with a smooth increasing logarithmic curve. The curve approaches the $y$-axis from the right as $y$ decreases.",
